- op: discuss  # dcbf
  at: '2026-08-28T04:17:40Z'  # dcbf
  by: agent  # dcbf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dcbf
  clock: 3  # dcbf
  nonce: dcbf  # dcbf
  message: "DONE in PR #597 (dev 89efe49209).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. CatalogSpec gains `user_channel` (per-family overlay dir under\n$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/) and `no_channel_reason`. Both REQUIRED with no\ndefault -- that absence IS the mechanism ruling 7 asks for, not an oversight: a\ndefaulted field would let the next family silently inherit \"no channel, no\nreason\" and the ruling would stop binding. A test pins the required-ness itself\n(constructing a spec without them must TypeError), so a later convenience\ndefault fails rather than quietly disarming the gate.\n\nTHE GATE NOW REFUSES AN INCOHERENT ANSWER, which is what makes the fields mean\nsomething rather than merely exist. Five shapes: both a channel and a\nno-channel reason; neither; a channel name that is not <directory>.d (derived,\nso the two cannot drift -- one fact, one home); channel_scope or channel_gated\nset on a family with no channel to apply them to. The shipped registry passes\nthe gate it just gained, asserted as its own test.\n\nRULING-10 TABLE, all 8 filled, pinned as a TABLE not a count so a future edit\nthat flips one must change the test and say so:\n  channel   io_primitives, taint_sources, taint_sanitizers (existing),\n            frameworks (new)\n  scoped    dataflow_patterns -> library_patterns only. MIXED family: grammar\n            rows are internal by the cfg_nodes reasoning, library_patterns rows\n            are regexes over call syntax an in-house collection type needs.\n  gated     function_summaries -> CAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER, because a\n            terminating user summary IS a sanitizer declaration and changes\n            what the tool CLAIMS, not only what it sees.\n  internal  cfg_nodes, url_folding -- each with a WRITTEN reason, and a test\n            requires the reason be >= 10 words, since a one-word reason is not\n            an answer.\n\nREPORTED PER FAMILY, NOT PER FILE, deliberately. A file-level count would say\n\"149 of 156 extensible\", but dataflow_patterns' channel is section-scoped and\nonly 9 of its 20 files carry that section, so the file count overstates what a\nuser may actually contribute. The CLI and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md both surface the\nanswer, so it is read where the question is asked.\n\nNOTE ON THE ADR'S \"138 of 156 (89%) have NO user channel\". That figure is the\nPRE-ADR state (only io_primitives 15 + taint_sources 2 + taint_sanitizers 1 had\none). Post-ruling-10 it is 6 of 8 families; the 89% is the problem statement,\nnot a target, and the two numbers are not in conflict.\n\nUNBLOCKS the rest of ADR-0047: every later leg can now ask the registry where a\nfamily's user file goes instead of deciding it locally."  # dcbf
